&lt;h4&gt;FACULTY FRONTLIST&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;frontlist: /ˈfrən(t)ˌlist/ &amp;nbsp;a list of books that is about to or has recently been published&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us at Book Culture&amp;#39;s 112th Street location for the inaugural reading in our new Undergraduate Creative Writing series, where we celebrate new releases from our esteemed faculty! Featuring readings from Adjunct Assistant Professors&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://arts.columbia.edu/directory/sophie-kemp"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sophie Kemp&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;23&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;(&lt;em&gt;Paradise Logic&lt;/em&gt;),&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://arts.columbia.edu/directory/anika-jade-levy"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anika Jade Levy&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;23&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;(&lt;em&gt;Flat Earth&lt;/em&gt;),&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://arts.columbia.edu/directory/melissa-lozada-oliva"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Melissa Lozada-Oliva&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;(&lt;em&gt;Candelaria; Beyond All Reasonable Doubt, Jesus Is Alive!&lt;/em&gt;), and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://arts.columbia.edu/directory/giada-scodellaro"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Giada Scodellaro&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;(&lt;em&gt;Some of Them Will Carry Me; Ruins, Child&lt;/em&gt;). Readings will be followed by a brief moderated conversation with Assistant Professor&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://arts.columbia.edu/node/1664"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hilary Leichter&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;12&lt;/strong&gt;,&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and an audience Q+A.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.bookculture.com/event/112th-creative-writing-faculty-reading-sophie-kemp-giada-scodellaro-melissa-lozada-oliva-and" target="_blank"&gt;Register&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Please join the East Central European Center, the Barnard Music Program, and the Columbia Music Department for a lunchtime performance of Eastern European chamber music. Organized by &lt;a href="https://harriman.columbia.edu/person/gail-archer/"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gail Archer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;***The IAB Publique Cafe will be a quiet space during this performance***&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please email&amp;nbsp;disability@columbia.edu&amp;nbsp;to request disability accommodations. Advance notice is necessary to arrange for some accessibility needs.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Stress&amp;nbsp;management,&amp;nbsp;sleep,&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;nutrition&amp;nbsp;are&amp;nbsp;key&amp;nbsp;elements&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;a&amp;nbsp;student&amp;rsquo;s&amp;nbsp;well-being. Participants will learn about why these behaviors are important, strategies for incorporating them into their lives, and resources available on campus that can provide support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Session&amp;nbsp;open&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;all&amp;nbsp;Columbia&amp;nbsp;University&amp;nbsp;students,&amp;nbsp;regardless&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;school&amp;nbsp;affiliation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note: This session will not be recorded, and slides are not shared. If you&amp;#39;re no longer able to attend, please remove your registration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Columbia University makes every effort to accommodate individuals with disabilities. If you require closed captioning, sign-language interpretation, or any other accommodation, please contact Disability Services at (212) 854-2388 or&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="mailto:disability@columbia.edu" target="_blank"&gt;disability@columbia.edu&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;at least 5 days in advance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Join University Life&amp;rsquo;s final event in our &lt;strong&gt;Make Space: A Self-Care Crafting Series&lt;/strong&gt; with &lt;strong&gt;Translucent &amp;amp; Tranquil&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Designed to help you slow down, get creative, and discover moments of intentional care, this session invites you to explore light and color through glass-inspired crafts. Different crafts include assembling pressed flower frames, glass magnets, and mosaic tile coasters &amp;mdash; each an opportunity to slow down and relax.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you can look forward to:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A peaceful space to create and unwind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All materials provided&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Light snacks to enjoy while you craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don&amp;rsquo;t forget to grab one of our self-care reflection books to track your progress throughout the rest of the semester. &lt;strong&gt;Return your book in May for a chance to win fun prizes.&lt;/strong&gt; Get creative this spring with fellow students while reducing stress, building confidence, and cultivating a steady self-care practice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All students are welcome. Entry is available on a first-come, first-served basis, while supplies last and until we reach capacity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Registration is encouraged, but not required. Please bring your CUID.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;What if I need accommodations?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; Columbia University makes every effort to accommodate individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodations to attend an event at Columbia University, please contact Disability Services (disability@columbia.edu or 212-854-2388) at least 10 days in advance of the event.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;*&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Will my photo be taken?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; Photographs and video may be taken at this event. ***By taking part in this event, you grant the organizers full rights to use the resulting images and to maintain in perpetuity copies of such recording in the collections of Columbia University. If you do not wish to be photographed, please inform an event organizer.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;By registering and attending this event, you agree to abide by the&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://universitypolicies.columbia.edu/content/rules-university-conduct"&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Rules of University Conduct&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
